WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.280
Supernatural monsters are&nbsp;
on the loose! Practitioners&nbsp;

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.280
of the Arcane Arts are here to bring about

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.720
the end of the world! Sinister paramilitary
forces are using paranormal objects to gain

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:16.720
an edge over their enemies! In short, things
are messed up, and when the anomalous is out

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.000
of line, we all know that there’s only one
group you’d ever think to call: The FBI’s

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.240
Unusual Incidents Unit.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.320
What, were you expecting someone else?

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:26.671
Everybody knows that the Unusual Incidents
Unit is the goto when it comes to paranormal

00:00:26.671 --> 00:00:31.120
deterrence. Sure, they don’t have the resources
of the SCP Foundation. They don’t have the

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.680
strategy of the Global Occult Coalition. They
don’t have the ruthlessness of the Chaos

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.640
Insurgency, or the arcane knowledge advantages
of the Serpent’s Hand. But they’ve gotta

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.840
have something, right? Right!?

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:49.040
Okay, maybe you’re not convinced, but you
will be! You may not respect them yet, but

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.040
you’ll change your tune when you find out
that the Unusual Incidents Unit has dealt

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:59.840
with one of the most important anomalies out
there: SCP-001. Or as the true experts over

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:07.280
at the UIU call it, CA3, short for “Confirmed
Anomaly 3.” If the evidence and files put

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.080
together by the UIU are to be believed - and
who are we kidding? Of course they are! - then

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.840
they may have the answer to one of the anomalous
world’s biggest questions: How was the SCP

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.400
Foundation actually formed?

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.280
But before we jump into the mysteries of CA3,
let’s talk a little bit more about the real

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.520
heroes of today’s story, the UIU. This secretive
offshoot of the FBI - America’s premier

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.480
domestic intelligence agency - was personally
commissioned by J. Edgar Hoover during the

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:42.080
Cold War. Why? For the same reason that literally
everything happened in the US during the Cold

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:47.440
War: To get an edge over the Soviets! Hoover
was an extraordinarily powerful man in US

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.960
politics, his tenure as FBI Director spanning
the terms of eight different presidents. If

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:57.600
he wanted to start a unit of agents whose
sole job was investigating the supernatural,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.080
nobody would dare stand in his way.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:05.600
Everyone always talks about the nuclear arms
race going on back in the 1960s, but far fewer

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:11.040
people talk about the supernatural arms race
that was happening at the exact same time.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.400
World War II coincided neatly with the Seventh
Occult War - an important geopolitical event

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:21.280
that played a huge role in shaping the Global
Occult Coalition - and a number of high-ranking

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.320
members of the Nazi party were believed to
be key figures in this secret, magical war.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.160
When the Soviets sacked a number of German
cities as part of their offensive campaigns

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.960
in World War II, they were able to bring back
scores of anomalous items that the Nazis had

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.000
been using to consolidate dark power. This
didn’t bode well for the United States Government

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.760
during the Cold War. After all, the only thing
scarier to them than Communists were Magical

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.800
Communists! The US needed to build up its
own anomalous arsenal, and that’s where

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.640
the UIU came in.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.080
The FBI allocated some of its okayest personnel
to the task. Most were either agents who had

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.320
experienced a paranormal encounter out in
the field, or who were being punished for

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.800
some kind of heinous mistake they’d made
carrying out their duties elsewhere. Despite

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:11.520
not being the best of the best, these agents
sure were eager to get their hands on some

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.480
cans.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:17.440
That isn’t an innuendo, by the way. The
Foundation refers to anomalies it deals with

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:24.640
as SCPs, or “Skips”, the GOC calls them
Parathreats, and the UIU calls them Cans,

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:30.080
again short for “Confirmed Anomalies.”
Well, when it’s an anomalous event or location,

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:35.200
anyway. Anomalous objects, like cursed books
or supernaturally powerful weapons, are referred

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:40.800
to as “Carts”, or “Confirmed Artifacts.”
And finally, anomalous people or sentient

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.880
entities are referred to by the unfortunate
name of “Can Man.”

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:49.920
It may not sound as cool, but hey, it gets
the job done just fine in the end.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.880
While the Unusual Incidents Unit may lack
the knowledge, strength, resources, and even

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.040
cred of its fellow groups of interest, that
doesn’t mean that it doesn’t keep track

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.840
of the others. In fact, the UIU has a pretty
unique relationship with each of them.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:09.520
The GOC, for example, is nicknamed “The
Suits” by the UIU. The official UIU orientation

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.520
states that the Suits outrank them, and if
they’re asked to follow an order by a member

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.480
of the Suits, they should just go ahead and
do it. Same goes for members of The Fireworks

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.240
- which is the UIU lingo for the Chaos Insurgency.
Unlike the Foundation, which generally has

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:29.760
the resources to go toe to toe with the Chaos
Insurgency, the UIU are rightfully terrified

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.720
of them. Official orders from the top are
for UIU agents to do whatever they say, or

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.680
they might find themselves getting shot in
the head by a Chaos Insurgent, or worse.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:45.040
Next, the Cart Shoppers, also known as Marshall,
Carter, and Dark, a sinister gentleman’s

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:50.720
club and auctioneer of anomalous items. Official
protocol is to raid any deals being conducted

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.256
by Marshall, Carter, and Dark, but oftentimes
these raids are unsuccessful, because M C

00:04:56.256 --> 00:05:00.960
and D’s security force are more competent
fighters than anyone on the Unusual Incidents

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.000
Unit Payroll.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.400
On the other end of the spectrum are The Can
Collection, the official UIU nickname for

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:11.600
the Serpent’s Hand. UIU Leadership recommends
against their agents staging any one-on-one

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:16.160
confrontations with them. Official memos also
contain the phrase “If they give you an

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.880
order, consider following it, they can probably
set you on fire with their mind.”

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.040
And finally, the most important relationship&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.480
of all is the one they have&nbsp;
with the SCP Foundation.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.040
Much like the rest of the groups of interest
on their roster, the UIU is subordinate to

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:36.240
the SCP Foundation, their agents happily taking
orders from them at the drop of a hat. They

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:41.760
call the Foundation the Skippers, but don’t
let the casual name fool you. The SCP Foundation

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:46.720
is so far above them on the pecking order
that they rarely even communicate in any official

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:47.600
capacity.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:52.160
When the Foundation talks to the UIU, it’s
always through code. They wouldn’t dream

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.120
of letting a hapless UIU agent help them on
any major operation, but lazier agents of

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:02.560
the Foundation might occasionally outsource
work to UIU agents. If ever one of these plucky

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.880
feds receives a message starting with, “Hey
Skipper”, they can be sure they’re about

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.080
to have a low-priority anomalous case pawned
off on them.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:13.680
The UIU are so subservient to the SCP Foundation&nbsp;

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.800
that it has sometimes&nbsp;
resulted in truly humiliating

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:22.240
mix-ups. One high-ranking member of the UIU
once took orders from a pizza delivery guy,

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:26.240
because he thought the pizzeria’s name,
the Spiced Crust Pizzeria, which could be

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.440
shortened to SCP was actually a coded plant
sent by the Foundation to deliver a message,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:36.720
rather than a deep dish pepperoni and cheese.
Incidents like this are why nobody takes the

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.320
UIU seriously.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:44.720
But according to them, there was a time before
all this. That time ended on September 7th,

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:52.320
1954, when CA3 - or SCP-001, as the Foundation
would later call it - first appeared on the

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:58.080
UIU’s radar. It seemed to be the most standard
Can you could possibly imagine: An anomalous

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.480
high school building causing a disturbance
in the suburbs of small town America.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.720
The UIU received the call after a number of
students claimed the interior of their school

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:11.360
suddenly looked completely different than
it ever had before, despite there being no

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:15.600
records of an official remodel. And we’re
not just talking about moving furniture and

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.280
a new coat of paint, either.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:23.200
The official CA3 file logs a number of changes.
These include, but are not limited to, all

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.520
the walls in the building&nbsp;
becoming steel-reinforced&nbsp;

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.840
concrete. All the windows being blacked out

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:33.120
from the inside. All student desks, personal
effects, textbooks, and any other standard

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.760
equipment left inside the&nbsp;
school simply disappearing&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.840
in the night. The entire floor plan of the

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:43.040
building seeming to have shifted, with rooms
altering in both dimensions and location,

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.840
as well as featuring&nbsp;
seemingly random modifications&nbsp;

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.320
within. None of this matched up the building’s

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:53.440
original blueprints, which were obtained by
the UIU shortly after the Can was reported.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:08:00.240
But things got even stranger for investigating
UIU agents. The building now contained seventeen

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:01.200
computers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:06.240
each with state-of-the-art magnetic-core
RAM and advanced cybersecurity. For a suburban

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:12.240
high school in 1954, it goes without saying
that this was extremely impressive. But weirdest

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:17.760
of all was the fact that a large and seemingly
impenetrable steel wall had appeared in the

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:22.960
auditorium, blocking it off and leaving whatever
was taking place on the other side a complete

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:28.000
mystery. Naturally, the UIU did what little
they could to investigate the matter.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:34.640
The first investigation group they sent inside
- Team CA3-O5 - never came back out. And Team

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:40.400
CA3-O6, the team they sent in to locate and
retrieve the first team, also disappeared

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:44.320
within the anomaly. Classic UIU expertise
at work.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:49.200
Almost a month after discovery and initial
containment, a strange noise began emanating

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.880
from the auditorium. Shortly after that, the
building became filled with people, all walking

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.840
around and working at different operations.
Eerily, everyone there had a resemblance to

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:06.720
members of Team CA3-O6, the rescue team sent
in to save the twelve members of CA3-05, all

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.280
of whom were still unaccounted for.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:14.640
Three months later, the strangeness escalated.
More noises came from the auditorium, and

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:18.800
the anomalous people inside the building had
gathered around the steel wall within. There

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:24.000
was a hole in the wall, six feet in diameter,
and every three minutes for several hours,

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.320
the people in the room would appear to simply
pull an anomalous object out of it.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.320
The items were then carried away, and placed&nbsp;

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.040
in one of the many rooms&nbsp;
that used to be classrooms,

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.720
before being locked up.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.360
The people within the building then seemed
to start guarding these strange items. Others

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:43.680
started performing tests, with what seemed
like far more advanced technology and methods

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:48.640
than what was possessed by the UIU during
the 1950s. What was going on here?

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:53.440
A few days later, several armed guards exited
the building and began guarding the perimeter.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:58.320
When UIU personnel attempted to lead an assault
on these guards, they were quickly overpowered,

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:03.440
even when advancing with vastly superior numbers.
Whether this was due to the skill of the guards

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:08.160
or the incompetence of UIU agents is still
very much an open question.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.320
Though strangely enough, intel bleeding out
from the inside confirmed that the people

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:17.200
within were treating their anomalous items
with UIU containment and testing protocols

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:22.480
- which is consistent with the knowledge that
CA3-O5 would have had. It seemed almost as

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:28.720
though O5, or copies of O5, were creating
a new splinter organization from within.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:34.480
And soon enough, it wasn’t just confined
to the interior of the CA3 building anymore.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:39.680
CA6, a Can Man that the UIU had been tracking
outside the school, was suddenly kidnapped

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:44.720
and shoved into a black car by two assailants
who appeared identical to Agent Dixon - a

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:50.800
man who’d been a member of Team CA3-O6.
The black car then returned to the CA3 facility,

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:55.680
and was allowed to enter into the complex
by the armed guards. CA6 was then removed

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:00.720
from the car by the Dixon clones, and placed
into containment in one of the classrooms.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:05.600
It wasn’t long after that that the anomalous
people within the CA3 facility made direct

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:12.400
contact with the UIU outside. They sent a
message in morse code on May 1st, 1965. The

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:17.360
people sending the message identified themselves
as the O5 Council - a name that seemed to

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:22.960
be taken directly from the O5 recon team sent
into the facility months ago. They identified

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:28.320
the new organization that they’d constructed
within the confines of the CA3 facility: The

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:33.840
SCP Foundation. They’d just opened their
very first containment site.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.480
This new Foundation expressed the desire to
become allies with the Unusual Incidents Unit,

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:43.680
but sadly for them, it was essentially the
last time they’d ever really be relevant.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.720
If this Foundation origin story is to be believed
- and as with all entries under the title

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:55.120
SCP-001, it’s worth taking it with a healthy
dose of skepticism - then the UIU witnessed

00:11:55.120 --> 00:12:00.560
the birth of the organization that would quickly
go on to outperform and overshadow them.

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:05.360
A big win for humanity in the quest to secure,
contain, and protect ourselves from dangerous

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.960
anomalies, but another L for the UIU.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:16.240
Now go check out “SCP-001 - Which is the
Real 001?” and “SCP-001 - When Day Breaks”

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:21.120
for more journeys into the endless mysteries
of SCP-001!

